# Local Docker Test Environment

`docker/docker-compose.yml` runs:

- DB service — MariaDB + `docker/init/*.sql` (schema, then privilege lockdown)
- Web service — PHP 5.4.45 Apache via `cyberpoison/php:5.4-apache`
  (`docker/Dockerfile` adds `pdo_mysql`; official `php:5.4.45-apache` is
  schema-1 and unusable on modern Docker), project root bind-mounted;
  published on host port **8080**. Local image tracks 5.4.45; production is
  5.4.16.

`docker/seed_junk_data.php` is mostly schema-driven (`INFORMATION_SCHEMA`).
A few physically bounded quantities are special-cased by column name; if those
columns are renamed, update that lookup in the seed.

Compose DB names/users/passwords are **local placeholders only** (same idea as
`includes/dbconnect-template.php` defaults). Do not commit real deployment
credentials. The web container reaches the DB over the compose network via
`SITE_DB_*` in compose.

After changing `docker/init/01_schema.sql`, recreate volumes so init re-runs
(`docker compose down -v && docker compose up -d --build` from `docker/`), then
reseed. A plain `up -d` leaves the old schema in place.

`docker compose` must be run from the directory that contains
`docker-compose.yml` — see `gotchas.mdc`.
